From f19768d1d49d733b4d522c114f6380b447b89413 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jatniel <noreply@example.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:23:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Show server dialogs (AuthMe 6's login) and answer them

AuthMe 6 logs players in with a native dialog, before they join and after. The
client ignored show_dialog, so the server waited for an answer that never came
while the client sat on the connecting screen.

dialog.rs reads a dialog (notice, confirmation, multi_action, server_links,
dialog_list; text, boolean, single_option and number_range inputs; custom,
run_command and nested-dialog actions), keeps what the player typed and builds
the answer. dialog_ui.rs places its parts on any screen size and finds what a
click hits. game/dialogs.rs shows it over everything, in the connecting phase or
in a world, takes the mouse, touch and keyboard (the system keyboard comes up
for a text input), and sends the answer as the configuration or play packet the
connection is in. Escape closes a dialog only when it says it can be closed.

Colors in a dialog's text are not shown yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
